@module entry
$8000 c Start ; JP Init: the entry Mover jumps to; its three bytes and the 181 after them are work space later
> After the start $8000-$8002 hold variables (MenuItem $8001, KeyItem $8000, WaitCount $8002-$8003) and $8000-$80B7 is the line buffer of the sprite routines (DrawShifted, DrawMirrored, BuildRoadRows: up to 184 bytes).
> Recorded: c1 frame 11646: Mover's JP $8000.
> Witness: L1 2 (c1, m128).
@alias KeyItem Start ; after the start: the item MenuSelect is on (also DEFINE KEYS' key being set)
@alias MenuItem Start+1 ; after the start: the main menu's item
@alias WaitCount Start+2 ; after the start: WaitKey's count (two bytes, over $8003)
@alias LineBuffer Start ; after the start: the sprite routines' line buffer $8000-$80B7
$8003 b InitialRecords ; The five stage records (99"59 each) and their total, copied to Records ($5E00) by Init
> 13 bytes: five times (seconds BCD, hundredths BCD) = $99, $59, then the total (minutes, seconds, hundredths) $03, $59, $96, which RecordTotals recomputes before it is shown. Afterwards the bytes are the line buffer.
@res tables/records.bin
$8010 s LineBufferTail ; $8010-$80B7: zeros, the rest of the sprite line buffer that starts at $8000
$80B8 c Init ; The IM 2 table, the records, the track tables, the bit-reverse table, the 128K test, IM 2 and on to Attract
> I = $B2, $B200-$B300 = $64; InitialRecords to Records ($5E00, 13 bytes); $EB00-$F0AF to StageList ($5E80, 1456 bytes: the stage list and the track); ReverseTable at $5D00 (each byte with its bits reversed, for DrawMirrored); the byte sum of ROM $3B00-$3BFF: $FE (the 48K ROM) gives Beeper = $FF, else 0; Players = 1; SP = 0 (the stack under $0000: $FFxx); IM 2; EI; falls into Attract.
> Recorded: c1 and m128 frame 11646; c1's sum is $FE, m128's is not: Beeper 0 there.
> Witness: L1 2 (c1, m128).
$80EC RomSum ; the 128K test: sum ROM $3B00-$3BFF
$80FE ; Beeper = $FF on the 48K ROM

@module menu ; The attract loop, the main menu, the control methods, DEFINE KEYS, the text printer, the keys
@about Attract wipes the screen and scrolls four credit lines up from the bottom (CreditList), then waits about 4 seconds (250 WaitKey units) for a key; with none it starts a demo race (DemoMode 8-15, the low bits of the distance) through NewGame. A key gives Menu: START GAME, ONE/TWO PLAYERS, CHANGE CONTROL MODE, DEFINE KEYS, chosen by MenuSelect (SPACE or fire picks, THROTTLE moves up, any other key down; about 22 seconds with no key go back to Attract).
@about The control methods (ControlTable, ControlMethod): 0 KEYBOARD (the keys of DEFINE KEYS, Q A O P SPACE by default), 1 KEMPSTON, 2 SINCLAIR RIGHT, 3 SINCLAIR LEFT, 4 CURSOR. PatchControls writes a method's five half-row bytes and masks into ReadControls' code (and DE = $FE20, or $1F28 for the Kempston: port $FE with JR NZ, or port $1F with JR Z); PAUSE (H) and RESET (R) are always keys. ReadControls returns D: bit 0 throttle, 1 wheelie, 2 left, 3 right, 4 brakes (fire), 5 pause, 6 reset.
@about The printer draws 8x8 characters of Font through RowTable (PrintChar: A the code, B the column, C the pixel line, E the attribute; B moves on), so the same code draws on the screen or, with RowTable pointing at it, into the back buffer.
$810C c Attract ; Wipe, scroll the credits up, wait for a key; none: a demo race; a key: Menu
> ClearScreen; ScrollPhase = 1; for each of the four CreditList records: the line printed centred at the bottom (pixel line 183), then ScrollUp the record's count of times, KeyOrFire stopping it into Menu. Then WaitKey with 250 units: a key gives Menu; none: DemoMode = 8 + (the distance AND 7) and NewGame plays a demo race.
> Recorded: c1: the credits from frame 11646; the demo from the attract in m128 and c1 before the menu key.
> Witness: L1 5 (c1, m128, names, stages).
$8160 ; the demo race (NewGame with DemoMode set)
$8163 c AttractScores ; After a demo: wait 200 units, show the high scores (ShowScores), wait 750 units, Attract again
> A key at either wait gives Menu. Known only from the code: no recording let a demo end (each pressed a key during it or before it).
$8178 c Menu ; The main menu: draw it, MenuSelect, then the item's action
> ClearScreen; DemoMode 0; MenuItem 0; the top four character rows' attributes $79; below them every attribute with a paper colour cleared to 0; the frame (FrameChars), MenuLayout's texts, ONE or TWO PLAYERS, MenuLayout2's texts. MenuSelect over MenuItems: timeout: Attract; 0: NewGame; 1: Players 1 <-> 2; 2: the method window (ControlItems, MenuSelect, ControlMethod, PatchControls); 3: DefineKeys.
> Recorded: c1, m128, ctl: every item; twoplayer: item 1.
@isub $817F LD (MenuItem),A
@isub $81E3 LD A,(MenuItem)
@isub $81F1 LD (MenuItem),A
@isub $824F LD (KeyItem),A
@isub $8280 LD A,(KeyItem)
