@module flow ; A game: the players' blocks and turns, a turn's screen, game over, the records, the lap table, the high scores and the name entry
@about NewGame clears both player blocks (Player, the current one at $5E0D, and OtherPlayer at $5E45, 56 bytes each), and the turn loop swaps them before each turn, skipping a player whose Timer is 0. With one player the second block's timer stays 0, so every turn is player 1's. PlayTurn draws the HUD and runs the race (JP StartRace); it returns at a fall's end (the timer still running: the next turn; a stage's end goes on to StageStart in the same turn) or at game over (Timer 0: the records, the lap table, the high score entry). With two players a key is waited for between turns (twoplayer). The game ends, back to Attract, when both timers are 0.
@about Times are BCD pairs: seconds (a value of $60 or more is one minute more) and hundredths. Records ($5E00) holds the five stage records and their total; a stage time shorter than its record replaces it at game over (RecordStages). The lap table shows the records beside the player's times, and for the stage the player did not finish the share of it driven, in %. The high score table (HiScores) has five rows of 22 characters: score, name and total time; a score above a row takes its place, the rows below move down, and the name is entered on a grid with the controls.
$8755 c NewGame ; Clear both player blocks, set the timers, the tracks and the countdowns, then the turn loop
> ClearScreen; $5E0D-$5E7C zero; both scores "      0"; outside a demo both countdowns 16; player characters '2' here and '1' in the other block (swapped at once by the loop); OtherPlayer's Timer = $60 and, with two players, Player's too; the track pointers TrackPtr = Track, the stage lists StageListPtr = StageList, the segment progress $80.
> Recorded: c1, m128: one player; twoplayer: both.
> Witness: L1 13 (c1, ctl, m128, stages, twoplayer).
$87BD TurnLoop ; swap the blocks (56 bytes); a player with Timer 0 is skipped
$87D9 ; the turn
$87E9 c TurnSkip ; The player's game is over but the other's is not: next turn
> Known only from the code: in twoplayer both games ended in the same round of turns.
$87EB TurnNext ; one player: on; two: Delay and GetKey first
$87FC c PlayTurn ; A turn: the HUD (frames, TOP, the best score, STAGE, TIME, SPEED, SCORE), JP StartRace; at game over the tables
> The pixel lines 0-63 cleared, their attributes $69; HudLayout's texts; two frames (FrameChars); DrawScore; the best score (HiScores' first row) at column 5; the stage in big digits; PrintTimer; SPEED 0; CALL GameEntry (JP StartRace). Back with Timer nonzero: RET (the next turn). Timer 0: the game is over: RecordStages, the totals (TotalTime = the player's finished stages, Records' total), the lap table (LapTable), then the high scores (ScoreCheck).
> Recorded: c1, m128: game over by the timer in stage 1; stages: game over after the finish; twoplayer: turns.
> Witness: L1 25 (c1, crash, ctl, fall5, m128, stages, truck, twoplayer).
