@module race ; A stage: the start, the pass loop, the countdown, the collisions, the HUD, the timer, the stage's end and the finish
@about StartRace (from PlayTurn, and again at each stage start) switches RowTable to the back buffer, sets the horizon and the stage's routines (StageParams patches the calls of RaceLoop and the off-road jump), colours the ground, places the riders (a new turn) and decodes the first segment; with Countdown bit 7 (after a fall) the bike resumes at FallX through GetUp.
@about RaceLoop is one pass: the countdown (16 passes of digits 3, 2, 1, GO in attribute blocks, beeps), PassCount + 1, ScrollStep = SPEED * 14, the AY effect, AdvanceTrack, ScrollBends, the row builder, the road, the ground's dots, MoveRiders (after the countdown), DrawRiders, BikeControl and DrawBike, the dust and the splash, the horizon's rotation, the object walk (draw and collide), the rider collisions, the HUD's flashing words, the copy to the screen and the horizon, the finish run, the score (the speed's digits each pass), the controls (pause, reset), the speed, the timer every 10 passes. c1's passes take 8.0 frames on average (6-12; 648 passes over frames 14075-19265); the heaviest (12 frames at 17143, 18151, 18911, 13 at 15169 with the crash noise) are passes with many rows and objects on screen or a sound effect (doc 04 4.6, 4.7).
@about The timer (Timer, BCD seconds) counts down once every 10 passes, so a "second" is 10 passes (about 80 frames); a stage's end adds 50 (at most 99) and shows EXTENDED PLAY; the time bonus puts the timer's tens and units as the 100 000s and 10 000s digits of the score: 10 000 points a second left. The stage's time (StageTime) is kept for the lap table. Game over is the timer at 0 with the bike stopped.
$A143 c CountGlyph ; Draw an 8-line glyph at HL as attribute blocks ($52) at DE (C lines: CountGlyphC)
> Witness: L1 32 (c1, crash, ctl, m128, names, stages, tech-brake-bend, tech-cheat, tech-land-wheelie, tech-ramp-wheelie, twoplayer).
$A145 c CountGlyphC ; The same with C preset (the digits' 10 lines)
> Witness: L1 616 (c1, crash, ctl, m128, names, stages, tech-brake-bend, tech-cheat, tech-land-wheelie, tech-ramp-wheelie, twoplayer).
$A15D b AyEffect ; The AY effect's five pairs: 7 = $07 (noise on A, B, C), 6 = $1F, volumes 8, 9, 10 = 15
@res tables/ayeffect.bin
$A167 c AyPairs ; Write E AY pairs from HL (as AyWrite, ports loaded each time)
> Witness: L1 1580 (c1, crash, fall5, m128, stages, tech-land-wheelie, tech-ramp-wheelie, truck, twoplayer).
$A179 c PlayEffect ; EffectTime = A (1 a fall, 2 a bounce or a landing), and the AY's noise on through AyEffect
> On the 48K the AY writes reach nothing; the 48K hears CrashSound instead.
> Witness: L1 316 (c1, crash, fall5, m128, stages, tech-land-wheelie, tech-ramp-wheelie, truck, twoplayer).
$A187 b StageParams 10 ; The five stages' routines: road, row builder, off-road, the ground's attribute, the copy mode, 2 bytes unused
> Stage 1: DrawRoad, RoadRowsCrest, OffRoad, $20; 2: the same, $30; 3: DrawRoad, RoadRowsJump, OffRoadSand, $28; 4: as 1, $70; 5: RoadNone, RoadRowsCrest, OffRoadStage5, $30. Byte 7 (BlitMode's JR) is 0 on all. src/res/tables/stageparams.csv.
@res tables/stageparams.bin
$A1B9 b CollisionSizes 2 ; Each object type's half width and height for the bike's collision (8 types): the ramp $20 x 1 ...
> Type 0 (ramp) 32 x 1, 1: 5 x 6, 2: 10 x 32, 3: 8 x 32, 4: 14 x 8, 5: 8 x 24, 6: 11 x 12, 7: 11 x 30. A hit within half the width is head-on (a fall at 35 km/h or more), else side-on (a bounce).
@res tables/collisions.bin

