@module race
$ABA1 c TrackStep ; Step HL to the track's next element and run the commands before it: marks, pattern calls and returns, jumps, the variable object
> HL is a track pointer, IX a track stack (TrackStack for the bike, the drawing walk's own), B the element's row for the marks. An element byte is a command (high nibble) and a gap (low nibble * 2: the distance from the previous element, in ScrollStep's high-byte units). $F0: a gap mark, its row into GapMarks (D, then E; 0 over the gap). $E0 ADDR, LEN: call the pattern at ADDR (a frame of 6 bytes: return, length, distance done) until LEN distance is driven. $D0: return from the pattern (the depth in IX+0). $C0 d: jump by d (signed) in the track. $B0+n: VarObject = 2n. Any other high nibble: an element (its type), and the distance is added to every open pattern's count; a pattern whose count reaches its length returns to its caller from that element, which is not placed: a call covers its elements below its length.
> Witness: L1 82250 (c1, crash, ctl, fall5, m128, names, stages, tech-brake-bend, tech-cheat, tech-land-wheelie, tech-ramp-wheelie, truck, twoplayer).
@isub $AE9E LD DE,$A55C
$AC0D ; a return with more than one frame open (not met: the track nests one level)
$AC3D ; an element: the distance into the open patterns
$AF2E c AdvanceTrack ; Each pass: BikeRoadPlace, then TrackDistance += ScrollStep; the elements passed (TrackStep); the segment's progress, and the next segment when it ends
> SegmentLeft counts down by ScrollStep; its high byte's change is RowsScrolled (ScrollBends). At the segment's end: SegmentLeft = the segment's length ($AF81: the segment byte's bits 6-7 + $80, in 256 units), and in a demo DemoMode - 1 (at 0 the demo ends: DemoEnd).
> Witness: L1 5203 (c1, crash, ctl, fall5, m128, names, stages, tech-brake-bend, tech-cheat, tech-land-wheelie, tech-ramp-wheelie, truck, twoplayer).
$AF81 SegmentLength ; ADD A,n: n = bits 6-7 of the segment (SegmentDecode)
$AF91 c DemoEnd ; The demo's segments used up: drop three returns and end the race (RaceEnd), back to the attract loop
> Known only from the code: every recorded demo was ended by a key first.
$AF97 c NextSegment ; Segments + 1, StageListPtr to the next segment; bit 5 of the one passed: the stage's end (StageEnd)
> Witness: L1 257 (c1, crash, fall5, m128, stages, tech-brake-bend, tech-cheat, tech-land-wheelie, tech-ramp-wheelie, truck, twoplayer).
$AFA7 c SegmentDecode ; The segment byte: Bend (bits 0-1, the bend), Crest (bits 2-3, the crest), BendDir (bit 4, the bend's side), length (bits 6-7); RoadRowsFlat when the crest was 0, ClearBendRows when the bend was 0
> Witness: L1 270 (c1, crash, ctl, fall5, m128, stages, tech-brake-bend, tech-cheat, tech-land-wheelie, tech-ramp-wheelie, truck, twoplayer).
$AFE0 c SetBendDir ; The bend's side into eight branch opcodes: JR NZ ($20) or JR Z ($28) at $9FAF, $93B7, $9680, $94A1, $94F5, $9AF5, $9B73, $9BB5
> Witness: L1 62 (c1, crash, ctl, fall5, m128, stages, tech-brake-bend, tech-cheat, tech-land-wheelie, tech-ramp-wheelie, truck, twoplayer).

@module bike
$AFFE c BikeRoadPlace ; From LateralX and the bend: patch the road's and the objects' centre into twelve operands, BikeX; OffRoad by stage
> The offset is clamped to +/-$21 (the rest goes to BikeX's offset); the operands at $93A0/$93A1, $9487/$9488, $94DA/$94DB, $9ADA/$9ADB, $9B59/$9B5A, $9B9D/$9B9E get ADD A,n or SUB n and the offset; $9F4F and $9643 the signed offset. In the air or falling no off-road test.
> Witness: L1 5265 (c1, crash, ctl, fall5, m128, names, stages, tech-brake-bend, tech-cheat, tech-land-wheelie, tech-ramp-wheelie, truck, twoplayer).
$B07A OffRoadJump ; JP nn: nn = StageParams' off-road routine (StartRace)

@module road
$B07D c ScrollBends ; As the segment moves (RowsScrolled), shift BendRows down and fill from the bend's profile (BendProfiles)
> Witness: L1 5198 (c1, crash, ctl, fall5, m128, names, stages, tech-brake-bend, tech-cheat, tech-land-wheelie, tech-ramp-wheelie, truck, twoplayer).
$B0C9 c ScrollBendsTail ; The profile's end reached inside the copy: the rest from BlendBend's start
> Known only from the code.
$B0D1 c BlendBend ; Bend 0 after a bend: BendRows blended back to straight, the profile's step from BendBlend ($75D7)
> Witness: L1 1756 (c1, crash, fall5, m128, stages, tech-brake-bend, tech-cheat, tech-land-wheelie, tech-ramp-wheelie, truck, twoplayer).
$B0FB c BlendCarry ; INC H: BendBlend's index crossing a page (not met)
> Known only from the code.
$B0FC ; the blend
$B11C b RowsScrolled ; The road rows the segment moved this pass (AdvanceTrack), for ScrollBends

@module graphics
$B11D b LeftoverCode ; $B11D-$B1FF: 227 bytes of an older build's code (LD ($B1BA),A ...), never run or read
> They disassemble as code addressing $B1xx; no instruction of the game points here and L1 has no run or read (the seven recordings).
$B200 b Im2Table 16 ; The IM 2 vector table, 257 bytes: Init fills it with $64 (vector $6464 = IntVector); the image holds older graphics here
$B301 b Gap5 ; 5 bytes between the table and the sprites ($90 $11 ...), never read
$B306 b Sprites ; The bike's, the riders', the trucks' and the splash and dust sprites ($B306-$E2BF), drawn through the descriptors
> BikePoses, RiderSprites, DrawSplash and DrawDust point into it. reset3's crash ran through $D253-$D26A as code (the bytes of a sprite); src/res/sprites/.
@res sprites/sprites.bin
$E2C0 b Dunes 32 ; Stage 3's horizon, 25 lines of 32 bytes
@res horizons/dunes.bin
$E5E0 b Mountains 32 ; Stages 1 and 4's horizon, 32 lines
@res horizons/mountains.bin
$E9E0 b Clouds 32 ; Stages 2 and 5's horizon, 9 lines
@res horizons/clouds.bin
$EB00 b TrackTables ; StageList, TrackPatterns and Track as loaded (1456 bytes): Init copies them to $5E80; then the back buffer's first rows
> $EB00-$EB8B StageList (140 segments), $EB8C-$ED4F the patterns, $ED50-$F0AF the track. src/res/track/ (tools/course.py draws each stage).
@res track/tables.bin
$F0B0 b OldGraphics ; $F0B0-$F5BF: 1296 bytes of older graphics under the back buffer, overwritten before any read
$F5C0 s BackBuffer ; $F5C0-$FDFF: zeros; the back buffer (lines 40-191) spans $EB00-$FDFF in play
$FE00 w RowTable 8 ; The address of each of the 192 pixel lines: the screen's, or the back buffer's after SetRowTable $A600
$FF80 b StackArea ; $FF80-$FFFF: the loader's leftovers (Stage0's copy, ROM glyphs); the game's stack below SP = 0
> Init sets SP = 0: the pushes go to $FFFF down (WALKTHROUGH 1: $FFE4-$FFFF used).
